==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Arugula.jpg|thumb|An arugula plant]]

===Etymology===
Probably {{etyl|it|en}} (dial. [[Lombardy]]) {{term|arigola|lang=it}}. (Eng. usg. 1967)

Cognate to {{term|rocket#Etymology 2|rocket|plant|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{enPR|əʹro͞ogələ}}, {{IPA|/əˈɹuɡələ/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/@"rug@l@/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|pl2=arugula}}

# A yellowish-flowered [[Mediterranean]] [[herb]] of the [[mustard]] family; which has flavoured leaves, often eaten in [[salad]]s. Has a distinct, [[peppery]] flavor.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|herb}} [[rugola]], [[rugula]], [[garden rocket]], [[rocket#Etymology 2|rocket]], {{taxlink|Eruca vesicaria|species}}

